      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Since 1912, the city has proudly used the slogan “World’s Safest Beach,” a claim that still echoes along its surf‑friendly shore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpinteria%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every year, locals and visitors celebrate the California Avocado Festival, a tradition that began in 1986 and showcases the region’s bounty.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpinteria%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Carpinteria Valley Historical Society runs a museum and research library that preserves the town’s rich heritage and archives.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
